d chromatic pc indices are the paper convention, not established ancient Hz or twelve-tone equal-tempered tuning."],"evidence":{"sourceId":"music:source:lam2024","normalizedTextChars":[27988,28498],"text":"To narrow the analytical object to modes only, rather than any kind of note, I will replace the symbols pos note and pc note with pos final and pc final , which denote the modal final as the analytical object in the subscript. Labeling modes: weidiao / zhidiao 為調之調. [4.2] Historically, pentatonic modes have been represented both as ( pc pent , pos final ) or ( pc final , pos final ). (18) Consider these two modes: for D, E, G, A, C, the pc pent is C, the pc final is D, and the pos final is shang , for C, "}},{"id":"chinese-expanded:lam:mode:0:0","nativeName":"0 set 宮 final","aliases":[],"unit":"Lam-source-defined-mode-final-context","tradition":"Chinese","witnessId":"Lam2024","position":{"generation":null,"sequence":null,"cyclicCoordinate":null,"orientation":null},"sourceRefs":["music:source:lam2024"],"assertionLayer":"source-rule-derived","exceptions":[],"pcPent":0,"posFinal":0,"pcFinal":0,"evidence":{"sourceId":"music:source:lam2024","normalizedTextChars":[27988,28498],"text":"To narrow the analytical object to modes only, rather than any kind of note, I will replace the symbols pos note and pc note with pos final and pc final , which denote the modal final as the analytical object in the subscript. Labeling modes: weidiao / zhidiao 為調之調. [4.2] Historically, pentatonic modes have been represented both as ( pc pent , pos final ) or ( pc final , pos final ). (18) Consider these two modes: for D, E, G, A, C, the pc pent is C, the pc final is D, and the pos final is shang , for C, "}},{"id":"chinese-expanded:lam:mode-tone:0:0:0","nativeName":"宮 in mode(0,0)","aliases":[],"unit":"mode-qualified-tone-membership-occurrence","tradition":"Chinese","witnessId":"Lam2024","position":{"generation":null,"sequence":null,"cyclicCoordinate":null,"orientation":null},"sourceRefs":